/* =====================================================================
   PICTURE BREAKDOWNS: every kanji made of parts is drawn with each part in its own colour,
   and each part gets a picture and its meaning, so you can see the kanji as a little scene.
   Original to this app: strokes from KanjiVG (CC BY-SA 3.0), part data from KanjiVG/Kanjium,
   stories from Make Me a Hanzi; the pictures are plain emoji.
   A part only gets a picture when the picture shows what its label says (目 eye, 木 tree, 車 car).
   Parts whose label is abstract or differs from what they once drew (自 self, 示 indicate, 方 direction) get none.
   ===================================================================== */
